 "ambiguities": [
  "F3 per-PMT gains are marginalised as a random gain (s_p^2 mu_p^2 added to every PMT variance) rather than profiled: one free gain per PMT is an incidental-parameter block that would make every other factor's profiled information exactly zero. s_p is the spread in force (lb.F3_SPREAD = 0.05), not the candidate spread of an F3 ceiling scan, because that is the F3 actually present in the simulated data.",
  "F2/F2' share the F1 module-gain nuisance block (the runbook's explicit joint profiling), so only their within-module variation survives; conservative.",
  "The across view used for the N_min check is a random module half, not the contiguous Hilbert half (view_masks is still a WP4c stub).",
  "F1 acceptance uses the main-cell (F2-free) ceiling; the joint F1/F2' row is recorded beside it for R11.",
  "Profiling is per event, not run-jointly; I_run = sum I_event is the registered approximation and biases the ceilings down.",
  "Dark counts are on for readout_pmt_r6: v_dark = 0.00109 PE^2 is the R-6 dark-charge variance derived from the reference manifest (1000 Hz x 1 us = 0.001 counts, each SPE-smeared by 1 + sigma_spe^2). It is a per-PMT white term, not a profiled nuisance.",
  "The fixed parity charge gain is detector response: it is part of mu here and in the nominal twin, so the twin cancels only the injected F1/F3 (and F2/F2'/R11b/T) gains."
